Planetary surface maps
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`data/textures/` holds surface, elevation, cloud and ring maps for the Solar
System, built by `apps/ingest` from published imagery. **Not covered by the
Apache License.** Per-file provenance is in `data/textures/manifest.json` and the
terms are in `data/textures/LICENSE.md`.

Most are public domain — NASA and USGS imagery is not subject to copyright:

  NASA Earth Observatory — Blue Marble Next Generation, Black Marble, GEBCO_08
  NASA Scientific Visualization Studio — LRO LROC color, LRO LOLA topography
  NASA / JPL / USGS Astrogeology Science Center — Voyager and Galileo global
    mosaics of Io, Europa, Ganymede and Callisto
  NASA / USGS Astrogeology Science Center — New Horizons global mosaics of Pluto
    and Charon, Dawn Framing Camera mosaics of Ceres and Vesta, and the Mars
    Express SRC mosaic of Phobos
  NASA / Goddard / University of Arizona (OSIRIS-REx), via USGS Astrogeology —
    the OCAMS global color mosaic of Bennu at 25 cm per pixel

The exceptions require attribution and impose no share-alike:

  Solar System Scope — https://www.solarsystemscope.com/textures/
  Maps of Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune and Saturn's
  rings. Licensed CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Modified: resized and re-encoded.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Shape models
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`data/shapes/` holds measured figures for twenty-five Solar System bodies that
gravity never rounded off, built by `apps/ingest` from models archived at the
NASA Planetary Data System Small Bodies Node.

These are United States Government works and are in the PUBLIC DOMAIN. There is
no license to comply with. What is recorded instead is PROVENANCE, which for a
shape model matters more than a license does: a body's figure is a measurement,
and a measurement with no citation is a guess. `data/shapes/manifest.json`
carries the source URL, the publication each model comes from, the reconstructed
volume against the original, and the output digest, for every file.

  P. C. Thomas — Viking, Galileo, NEAR and Cassini shape models of Phobos,
    Deimos, Vesta, Ida, Gaspra, Mathilde, Hyperion, Janus and Epimetheus
  P. J. Stooke — the small-body map atlas: Amalthea, Thebe, Proteus, Larissa,
    Prometheus, Pandora, and the nucleus of 1P/Halley
  R. W. Gaskell — stereophotoclinometry models of 433 Eros and 25143 Itokawa
  PDS Small Bodies Node radar shape model compilation — 216 Kleopatra,
    4179 Toutatis, 1620 Geographos, 6489 Golevka, 4769 Castalia and 1998 KY26
  NASA / OSIRIS-REx / University of Arizona — the SPC/OLA global model of
    101955 Bennu at 6.32 m per facet

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Solar System measurements
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`packages/universe/src/solar/` carries the Solar System's published
measurements transcribed into source, and `data/reference/solar-system.json`
carries the same numbers fetched from JPL so the transcription can be checked
against them. Both are facts rather than a licensed database.

  NASA/JPL-Caltech Solar System Dynamics — planetary and satellite physical
    parameters, satellite mean elements, and the Small-Body Database.
    https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/ — public domain.

